{"name":"Ramjet","hex":"#4c73af","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ramjet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A jet engine in which forward motion forces air into an inlet, compressing it (as opposed to having a pump type device compressing the air for combustion with fuel), and where combustion is subsonic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ramjet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ramjet","blocks":[{"text":"A ramjet is a form of airbreathing jet engine that requires forward motion of the engine to provide air for combustion. Ramjets work most efficiently at supersonic speeds around Mach 3 and can operate up to Mach 6."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Ramjet_operation.svg/330px-Ramjet_operation.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramjet","wikidata":"Q60602"},{"title":"Ramjet (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Ramjet is a Japanese Thoroughbred racehorse. He has competed since 2023, recording five wins in seventeen starts, including the Tokyo Derby (JpnI) and Unicorn Stakes (GIII) in 2024. His racing name is derived from the ramjet, a type of jet engine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/%E3%83%A9%E3%83%A0%E3%82%B8%E3%82%A7%E3%83%83%E3%83%88_%E6%9D%B1%E4%BA%AC%E3%83%80%E3%83%BC%E3%83%93%E3%83%BC%E5%85%A5%E7%B7%9A%E6%99%82.jpg/330px-%E3%83%A9%E3%83%A0%E3%82%B8%E3%82%A7%E3%83%83%E3%83%88_%E6%9D%B1%E4%BA%AC%E3%83%80%E3%83%BC%E3%83%93%E3%83%BC%E5%85%A5%E7%B7%9A%E6%99%82.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramjet_(horse)","wikidata":"Q130350385"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Leduc_010_Ramjet_Prototype_%2811729010226%29.jpg/500px-Leduc_010_Ramjet_Prototype_%2811729010226%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia